{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Backpropagation from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: The Value Node"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every number in our computation becomes a Value. It stores its data, its gradient, and how it was created (so it knows how to compute gradients backward)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Value:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, data, children=(), op=''):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.data = data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.grad = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._backward = lambda: None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._children = set(children)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._op = op"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __repr__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return f\"Value(data={self.data:.4f}, grad={self.grad:.4f})\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "No gradient yet (0.0). No backward function yet (no-op). The `_children` track which Values produced this one, so we can topologically sort the graph later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Operations with Backward Functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each operation creates a new Value and defines how gradients flow backward through it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def __add__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    other = other if isinstance(other, Value) else Value(other)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = Value(self.data + other.data, (self, other), '+')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.grad += out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        other.grad += out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def __mul__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    other = other if isinstance(other, Value) else Value(other)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = Value(self.data * other.data, (self, other), '*')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.grad += other.data * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        other.grad += self.data * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For addition: d(a+b)/da = 1, d(a+b)/db = 1. So both inputs get the output's gradient directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For multiplication: d(a*b)/da = b, d(a*b)/db = a. Each input gets the other's value times the output gradient."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `+=` is critical. A Value might be used in multiple operations. Its gradient is the sum of gradients from all paths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Sigmoid and Loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = self.data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = max(-500, min(500, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = Value(s, (self,), 'sigmoid')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.grad += (s * (1 - s)) * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Sigmoid derivative: sigmoid(x) * (1 - sigmoid(x)). We computed sigmoid(x) = s during the forward pass. Reuse it. No extra work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mse_loss(predicted, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    diff = predicted + Value(-target)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return diff * diff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "MSE for a single output: (predicted - target)^2. We express subtraction as addition with a negated Value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Backward Pass"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Topological sort ensures we process nodes in the right order -- a node's gradient is fully accumulated before we propagate through it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def backward(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    topo = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    visited = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def build_topo(v):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if v not in visited:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            visited.add(v)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for child in v._children:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                build_topo(child)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            topo.append(v)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    build_topo(self)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    self.grad = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for v in reversed(topo):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v._backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Start at the loss (gradient = 1.0, since dL/dL = 1). Walk backward through the sorted graph. Each node's `_backward` pushes gradients to its children."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Layer and Network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Neuron:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_inputs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scale = (2.0 / n_inputs) ** 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.weights = [Value(random.uniform(-scale, scale)) for _ in range(n_inputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bias = Value(0.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        act = sum((wi * xi for wi, xi in zip(self.weights, x)), self.bias)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return act.sigmoid()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.weights + [self.bias]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Layer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_inputs, n_outputs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.neurons = [Neuron(n_inputs) for _ in range(n_outputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = [n(x) for n in self.neurons]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out[0] if len(out) == 1 else out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for n in self.neurons:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            params.extend(n.parameters())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Network:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, sizes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.layers = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(sizes) - 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.layers.append(Layer(sizes[i], sizes[i + 1]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for layer in self.layers:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = layer(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if not isinstance(x, list):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                x = [x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x[0] if len(x) == 1 else x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for layer in self.layers:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            params.extend(layer.parameters())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def zero_grad(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p in self.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p.grad = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A Neuron takes inputs, computes weighted sum + bias, and applies sigmoid. Weight initialization scales by sqrt(2/n_inputs) to prevent sigmoid saturation in deeper networks. A Layer is a list of Neurons. A Network is a list of Layers. The `parameters()` method collects all learnable Values so we can update them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Train on XOR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = Network([2, 4, 1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "xor_data = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0.0, 0.0], 0.0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0.0, 1.0], 1.0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1.0, 0.0], 1.0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1.0, 1.0], 0.0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "learning_rate = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for epoch in range(1000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_loss = Value(0.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for inputs, target in xor_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = [Value(i) for i in inputs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss = mse_loss(pred, target)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_loss = total_loss + loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    net.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in net.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p.data -= learning_rate * p.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if epoch % 100 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"Epoch {epoch:4d} | Loss: {total_loss.data:.6f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\nXOR Results:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, target in xor_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = [Value(i) for i in inputs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {pred.data:.4f} (expected {target})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Watch the loss decrease. From random predictions to correct XOR outputs, driven entirely by backpropagation computing gradients and nudging weights in the right direction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Circle Classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In Lesson 02, you hand-tuned weights for circle classification. Now let the network learn them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "random.seed(7)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def generate_circle_data(n=100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    data = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x1 = random.uniform(-1.5, 1.5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x2 = random.uniform(-1.5, 1.5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        label = 1.0 if x1 * x1 + x2 * x2 < 1.0 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data.append(([x1, x2], label))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "circle_data = generate_circle_data(80)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "circle_net = Network([2, 8, 1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "learning_rate = 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for epoch in range(2000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.shuffle(circle_data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_loss_val = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for inputs, target in circle_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = [Value(i) for i in inputs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = circle_net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss = mse_loss(pred, target)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        circle_net.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p in circle_net.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p.data -= learning_rate * p.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_loss_val += loss.data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if epoch % 200 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for inputs, target in circle_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = [Value(i) for i in inputs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pred = circle_net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            predicted_class = 1.0 if pred.data > 0.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if predicted_class == target:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        accuracy = correct / len(circle_data) * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"Epoch {epoch:4d} | Loss: {total_loss_val:.4f} | Accuracy: {accuracy:.1f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We use online SGD here -- update weights after each sample instead of accumulating the full batch. This breaks symmetry faster and avoids sigmoid saturation on the full loss landscape. Shuffling the data each epoch prevents the network from memorizing the order."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "No hand-tuning. The network discovers the circular decision boundary on its own. That's the power of backpropagation: you define the architecture, the loss function, and the data. The algorithm figures out the weights."
      ]
    },
